// Default Antigravity settings for aetherion antigravity-ide namespaces.
//
// Seed file (skeleton dotfile per STYLE.md): copied into the
// namespace's $HOME on first launch and frozen there. Edits the user
// makes inside the namespace win; rebuilding the image does NOT
// refresh this file (use `aetherion reset namespace <name>` if you
// want to drop user changes and reseed).
//
// Antigravity is a VS Code / Code-OSS fork — settings keys mirror
// upstream VS Code, read from ~/.config/Antigravity/User/settings.json
// (the "Antigravity" capitalization is what the .deb's product name
// resolves to on Linux). Project-level overrides at
// <project>/.vscode/settings.json still apply on top.
//
// Three intentional defaults — everything else stays at upstream:
//
//   - telemetry.telemetryLevel: "off"
//       Antigravity inherits VS Code's telemetry pipeline AND ships
//       Google's own usage reporting on top (Cascade sessions,
//       agent-tool invocations). Aetherion namespaces are ephemeral
//       build sandboxes; both pings would just be noise. Opt back in
//       per-namespace if you want.
//
//   - update.mode: "none"
//   - update.showReleaseNotes: false
//       Image-managed install via the apt repo. In-namespace updates
//       would either fail (no apt-get from the unprivileged user) or
//       drift the install away from the pinned image build. Refresh
//       by rebuilding the image with a newer ANTIGRAVITY_VERSION
//       build arg (or unpinning to track the apt repo's latest).
//
//   - extensions.autoUpdate: false
//   - extensions.autoCheckUpdates: false
//       Same rationale: extensions live in $HOME and survive
//       rebuilds, but silent background updates while you're working
//       drag in network and surface unexpected breakage. Use the
//       Extensions view to update on demand.
{
  "telemetry.telemetryLevel": "off",
  "update.mode": "none",
  "update.showReleaseNotes": false,
  "extensions.autoUpdate": false,
  "extensions.autoCheckUpdates": false
}
